{"id":"transplant","cards":[{"id":"transp038b3f3d","l":2,"f":"Transplants that need <b>immunosuppression</b>","b":"<b>liver, kidney, heart, small intestine</b> (not cornea, tendon, skin, bone, heart valves)","c":"Introduction › Definition & Basic Concepts"},{"id":"transp479bddaa","l":2,"f":"Excludes a cadaveric liver donor → <b>active systemic bacterial infection</b> ; brain-dead 62-year-old wanting to donate","b":"contraindicated by <b>history of melanoma</b> (age &gt; 60 and steroids are not absolute)","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transpfd6ccbdf","l":2,"f":"Na <b>190</b> for 48 h in a brain-dead donor","b":"keyed <b>exclude kidney, pancreas and liver</b> (severe hypernatraemia &gt; 170 damages grafts)","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp14dae52b","l":1,"f":"<b>Origins</b> — Milestone?","b":"<b>Alexis Carrel</b> — vascular anastomosis techniques (Nobel Prize)","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp721c1b86","l":1,"f":"<b>World War I</b> — Milestone?","b":"Early skin transplantation","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp422e0e09","l":1,"f":"<b>1953</b> — Milestone?","b":"Transplant immunology/immunosuppression increasingly understood","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp3baeb6b8","l":1,"f":"<b>1954</b> — Milestone?","b":"First successful <b>kidney transplant between identical twins</b> — no immunosuppression; graft function ~8 years","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp743110ea","l":1,"f":"<b>1958</b> — Milestone?","b":"<b>HLA</b> described","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transpe5340dbb","l":1,"f":"<b>1962</b> — Milestone?","b":"Successful kidney transplant from a <b>deceased donor</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp644ef624","l":1,"f":"<b>1963</b> — Milestone?","b":"Early <b>brain-dead donor</b> organ retrieval","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp1a7f00e7","l":1,"f":"<b>1967</b> — Milestone?","b":"Successful <b>liver transplantation</b> — <b>Thomas Starzl</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp54662681","l":1,"f":"<b>1981</b> — Milestone?","b":"Successful combined <b>heart-lung</b> transplantation","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transpb1c97550","l":1,"f":"<b>1983</b> — Milestone?","b":"<b>Cyclosporine</b> → markedly ↑ success; later <b>tacrolimus</b> and <b>MMF</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp212cd1a8","l":1,"f":"<b>1999</b> — Milestone?","b":"Pancreatic <b>islet-cell transplantation</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp9e22eaf0","l":1,"f":"<b>Types of Grafts</b> — Milestone?","b":"Legislation subsequently prohibited <b>buying/selling human organs</b>.","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp199171bc","l":1,"f":"<b>Autograft</b> — Donor → Recipient?","b":"<b>Same individual</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp06604861","l":1,"f":"<b>Autograft</b> — Notes?","b":"Skin graft, hair transplant; minimal immunologic complications","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transpc89d90ba","l":1,"f":"<b>Syngeneic</b> — Donor → Recipient?","b":"<b>Genetically identical</b> individuals","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp62577a64","l":1,"f":"<b>Syngeneic</b> — Notes?","b":"Identical twins","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp0559e80b","l":1,"f":"<b>Allograft</b> — Donor → Recipient?","b":"Different individuals, <b>same species</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp5316c112","l":1,"f":"<b>Allograft</b> — Notes?","b":"<b>Most common</b> solid-organ transplant","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transpff464b61","l":1,"f":"<b>Xenograft</b> — Donor → Recipient?","b":"<b>Different species</b>","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transpadb1bf40","l":1,"f":"<b>Xenograft</b> — Notes?","b":"Experimental — animal organs as temporary extracorporeal support","c":"History of transplantation"},{"id":"transp21c972c6","l":2,"f":"Kidney from an <b>identical-twin sister</b>","b":"<b>isograft</b>","c":"Types of grafts"},{"id":"transp2664846e","l":1,"f":"<b>Class I</b> — Expression?","b":"<b>Most nucleated cells</b>","c":"Immunology › Transplant Immunology"},{"id":"transp6d6e8e23","l":1,"f":"<b>Class II</b> — Expression?","b":"Primarily <b>antigen-presenting cells</b> (lymphocytes/macrophages)","c":"Immunology › Transplant Immunology"},{"id":"transp7bb3bdc4","l":1,"f":"<b>Hyperacute</b> — Timing?","b":"<b>Minutes–hours</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transpb1fc1ebb","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute</b> — Timing?","b":"<b>Days–weeks</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transp9b9b0388","l":1,"f":"<b>Chronic</b> — Timing?","b":"<b>&gt;6 months</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transpd189a775","l":1,"f":"<b>Hyperacute</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>Preformed recipient antibodies</b> (prior sensitization) vs <b>HLA/ABO</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transpa5e4f4d2","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute</b> — Mechanism?","b":"<b>T-cell mediated</b> (most common) or antibody- mediated","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transp39c781a2","l":1,"f":"<b>Chronic</b> — Mechanism?","b":"Gradual progressive decline in function","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transp59d4434b","l":1,"f":"<b>Hyperacute</b> — Key point?","b":"Antibody-mediated → aggressive, hard to suppress","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transp240a8aa8","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute</b> — Key point?","b":"<b>Most common</b>; <b>reversible</b> if treated early","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transpe77ddeab","l":1,"f":"<b>Chronic</b> — Key point?","b":"Histology distinguishes from acute","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transp63793fe2","l":1,"f":"<b>Hyperacute</b> — Management?","b":"Detect in pre-transplant matching; <b>plasmapheresis +</b> <b>IVIG</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transpb8bee617","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute</b> — Management?","b":"Diagnosis by <b>graft biopsy</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transp6ec93613","l":2,"f":"Kidney recipient unstable (hyperthermia, tachycardia) <b>in the recovery room/at closure</b> with <b>no arterial flow</b>","b":"<b>hyperacute rejection</b> — <b>pre-existing antibodies against donor proteins</b>","c":"Rejection"},{"id":"transpf7d11119","l":2,"f":"Drug used for <b>induction</b>","b":"<b>antithymocyte globulin</b>","c":"Immunosuppression"},{"id":"transp3ac0ebaf","l":2,"f":"Lung recipient on prednisone + a drug that <b>inhibits T-cell activation</b> → <b>cyclosporine</b> ; cyclosporine's mechanism → <b>inhibits T-cell activation</b> (calcineurin inhibitor","b":"↓ IL-2 transcription)","c":"Immunosuppression"},{"id":"transp5ca66dbe","l":2,"f":"<b>Absolute contraindication</b> to kidney transplantation","b":"<b>active malignancy</b>","c":"Immunosuppression › Compatibility & Immunosuppression"},{"id":"transp09951c8b","l":2,"f":"Tell a patient on immunosuppression","b":"↑ <b>squamous cell carcinoma</b> (infection IS dose-related)","c":"Immunosuppression complications"},{"id":"transp47bf7f5d","l":1,"f":"<b>Infection</b> — Details?","b":"<b>Correlates with intensity/dose.</b> First month → <b>bacterial</b>; viral → especially <b>CMV</b>; fungal also occur","c":"Immunosuppression complications"},{"id":"transp531e1ccb","l":1,"f":"<b>Malignancy</b> — Details?","b":"↑ risk, including <b>Kaposi sarcoma</b>","c":"Immunosuppression complications"},{"id":"transp2f3279a2","l":2,"f":"Heart-valve replacement from a circulatory-death donor","b":"<b>no immunosuppression needed</b>","c":"Organ donation"},{"id":"transp1569a56a","l":2,"f":"Colon cancer cured 20 years ago wanting to donate a kidney","b":"keyed <b>cannot donate</b> (history of malignancy) ; <b>primary brain tumours</b> (low-grade glioma, glioblastoma) are the exception — they <b>can</b> donate (rare extracranial spread)","c":"Organ donation"},{"id":"transp94b74d9c","l":1,"f":"<b>Living Donation</b> — Donor?","b":"Healthy person (<b>kidney, liver</b>)","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transpfc8baddf","l":1,"f":"<b>DBD</b> — Donor?","b":"<b>Brain death</b> — irreversible loss of brainstem function","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transpcbef90ba","l":1,"f":"<b>DCD</b> — Donor?","b":"Devastating brain injury, <b>not</b> meeting brain- death criteria","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp47e1dc85","l":1,"f":"<b>Living Donation</b> — Graft quality?","b":"<b>Higher</b> — donor extensively evaluated","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transpb4c53463","l":1,"f":"<b>DBD</b> — Graft quality?","b":"Good; may be judged only at surgery","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp4c3755f6","l":1,"f":"<b>DCD</b> — Graft quality?","b":"<b>Lower than DBD</b> — warm ischemia","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp97c1114e","l":1,"f":"<b>Living Donation</b> — Timing?","b":"<b>Elective</b> — planned, scheduled, optimally prepared","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp4ca6b4ba","l":1,"f":"<b>DBD</b> — Timing?","b":"Unpredictable","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp2970df03","l":1,"f":"<b>DCD</b> — Timing?","b":"After withdrawal of support","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp80b99be0","l":1,"f":"<b>Living Donation</b> — Key issue?","b":"Donor morbidity/mortality; <b>ethical/legal</b> (no organ sales)","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp4a25ac60","l":1,"f":"<b>DBD</b> — Key issue?","b":"Exclude reversible mimics","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp10f67dda","l":1,"f":"<b>DCD</b> — Key issue?","b":"<b>Warm ischemic time</b>","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp5674b48f","l":1,"f":"<b>Living Donation</b> — from a healthy person.?","b":"<b>Donation After Circulatory Death (DCD)</b>","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transpcf79372f","l":1,"f":"<b>DBD</b> — from a healthy person.?","b":"Living donation is a <b>major source</b> of transplants in the Middle East and parts of Asia; it is technically demanding because an organ/part is removed","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transpd7184257","l":2,"f":"Clinical brain death","b":"<b>no gag, corneal or cough reflex, no pupil response, no breathing</b>","c":"Deceased donation › Organ Donation"},{"id":"transp57e95ac2","l":2,"f":"True about liver transplant","b":"<b>5-year survival &gt; 75%</b> (not heterotopic, no HLA matching)","c":"Kidney transplantation"},{"id":"transped1770db","l":2,"f":"Rejection <b>6 years</b> after transplant → <b>chronic</b> ; non-compliant kidney recipient with ↓ urine","b":"assess rejection by <b>graft biopsy</b>","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transp4234e0e0","l":1,"f":"<b>General</b> — Examples?","b":"Bleeding · infection · wound dehiscence","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transpfb870344","l":1,"f":"<b>Specific</b> — Examples?","b":"<b>Arterial thrombosis · venous thrombosis · urine leak · ureteric stricture · lymphocele</b>; kidney is highly immunogenic → substantial <b>rejection</b> risk","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transpba39e5d7","l":1,"f":"<b>Living donor</b> — 1-Year?","b":"<b>~98%</b>","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transp5ff1184f","l":1,"f":"<b>Living donor</b> — 5-Year?","b":"<b>~80%</b>","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transp331eca82","l":1,"f":"<b>Deceased (brain-dead) donor</b> — 1-Year?","b":"<b>~95%</b>","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transpa81a69b6","l":1,"f":"<b>Deceased (brain-dead) donor</b> — 5-Year?","b":"<b>~70%</b>","c":"Kidney transplantation › Kidney Transplantation"},{"id":"transp7e62e5fb","l":1,"f":"<b>Enteric</b> — Technique?","b":"Donor duodenum → recipient <b>small bowel</b>","c":"Pancreas Transplant › Pancreas Transplantation"},{"id":"transp657a5631","l":1,"f":"<b>Enteric</b> — Consequence?","b":"Secretions enter GI tract <b>physiologically</b>","c":"Pancreas Transplant › Pancreas Transplantation"},{"id":"transp7fb94529","l":1,"f":"<b>Bladder</b> — Technique?","b":"Extraperitoneal; donor duodenum → <b>urinary bladder</b>","c":"Pancreas Transplant › Pancreas Transplantation"},{"id":"transp792baeff","l":1,"f":"<b>Bladder</b> — Consequence?","b":"Bicarbonate-rich secretions lost in urine → <b>metabolic acidosis</b>","c":"Pancreas Transplant › Pancreas Transplantation"},{"id":"transpd15366ef","l":1,"f":"<b>• Bleeding · infection • Pancreatic leak •</b> — Technique?","b":"• • Metabolic acidosis (bladder drainage) •","c":"Pancreas Transplant › Pancreas Transplantation"},{"id":"transp30c6221e","l":1,"f":"<b>• Bleeding · infection • Pancreatic leak •</b> — Consequence?","b":"• <b>Arterial/venous thrombosis</b> • <b>Graft pancreatitis</b> • High risk of <b>rejection</b>","c":"Pancreas Transplant › Pancreas Transplantation"},{"id":"transp3a3174f5","l":2,"f":"<b>Contraindication</b> to liver transplantation","b":"<b>cirrhosis with ongoing substance abuse</b>","c":"liver transplant › Liver Transplantation"},{"id":"transp1a80122d","l":2,"f":"Child C liver disease → <b>liver transplant</b> ; 4-cm HCC with Child B → <b>liver transplant</b> (Milan) ; autoimmune hepatitis (incomplete recall)","b":"<b>liver transplant</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp9554b3d6","l":1,"f":"<b>Kidney / Pancreas</b> — HLA matching?","b":"<b>Required</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transpf8c9914e","l":1,"f":"<b>Liver</b> — HLA matching?","b":"<b>Not routinely required</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp056e8eef","l":1,"f":"<b>Kidney / Pancreas</b> — Immunogenicity?","b":"Highly immunogenic","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp02966c88","l":1,"f":"<b>Liver</b> — Immunogenicity?","b":"Relatively <b>less immunogenic</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp5d21852c","l":1,"f":"<b>Kidney / Pancreas</b> — ABO?","b":"Compatible","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp58cf17d5","l":1,"f":"<b>Liver</b> — ABO?","b":"Compatible standard; <b>ABO-incompatible</b> possible in life-threatening cases with intensified immunosuppression","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transpd9f28e89","l":1,"f":"<b>Kidney / Pancreas</b> — Combined grafts?","b":"SPK: pancreas may protect kidney","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp5e8a04ac","l":1,"f":"<b>Liver</b> — Combined grafts?","b":"<b>Liver-kidney</b>: reduces kidney rejection risk","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp2c85adcd","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute liver failure</b> — Details?","b":"Drug toxicity — <b>paracetamol/acetaminophen</b>; viral causes","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp97756c8e","l":1,"f":"<b>Hepatic artery thrombosis</b> — Details?","b":"<b>Major post-transplant vascular complication</b> → acute graft failure","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp36218cbd","l":1,"f":"<b>Primary nonfunction</b> — Details?","b":"New liver fails without clear rejection; cause may remain uncertain → often <b>urgent retransplantation</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp527b8d90","l":1,"f":"<b>1. Hepatic artery</b> — Reconstruction?","b":"<b>Artery-to-artery</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp21fec410","l":1,"f":"<b>2. Portal vein</b> — Reconstruction?","b":"<b>Vein-to-vein</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp9c7a0b7f","l":1,"f":"<b>3. Hepatic venous/IVC outflow</b> — Reconstruction?","b":"<b>Caval replacement</b> or <b>piggyback</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp448d7df6","l":1,"f":"<b>4. Bile duct</b> — Reconstruction?","b":"Healthy duct → <b>duct-to-duct</b>; unsuitable/diseased → <b>hepaticojejunostomy</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp13ba33be","l":1,"f":"<b>Pediatric</b> — Graft Needed?","b":"<b>Segments II–III</b> may suffice","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transpb7c4b616","l":1,"f":"<b>Adult</b> — Graft Needed?","b":"Approximately <b>half the liver</b>, depending on sizes","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transpdf137592","l":1,"f":"<b>Complications &amp; Outcome</b> — Graft Needed?","b":"8 Couinaud segments (<b>segment I = caudate</b>). Donor hepatectomy must preserve structures and leave an <b>adequate remnant</b> for the healthy donor. Reconstruction: hepatic vein <b>vein-to-vein</b>, portal vein, biliary drainage may need <b>small bowel</b>.","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp4be03154","l":1,"f":"<b>General</b> — Complications?","b":"Bleeding · infection · wound complications/dehiscence","c":"Acute liver failure"},{"id":"transp29471bd7","l":1,"f":"<b>Specific</b> — Complications?","b":"<b>Primary graft nonfunction · hepatic artery thrombosis</b> · venous thrombosis · <b>bile leak</b> · biliary stricture · <b>ischemic cholangiopathy</b>","c":"Acute liver failure"}]}